<title>UK: Novorossiisk oil port reopens after thunderstorms.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil port reopens after thunderstorms.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk was operating normally on Friday having been closed twice on Thursday due to thunderstorms, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port was closed at 9 a.m. local time for over two hours and for about the same length of time in the late evening, the source said.</p>
<p>Two crude tankers and a gas oil tanker were alongside on Friday morning.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
